{
  "sn48.50:0.1": "Linked Discourses 48.50 ",
  "sn48.50:0.2": "5. Old Age ",
  "sn48.50:0.3": "At Āpaṇa ",
  "sn48.50:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn48.50:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Aṅgas, near the Aṅgan town named Āpaṇa. ",
  "sn48.50:1.3": "Then the Buddha said to Venerable Sāriputta: ",
  "sn48.50:1.4": "“Sāriputta, would a noble disciple who is sure and devoted to the Realized One have any doubt or uncertainty about the Realized One or his instructions?” ",
  "sn48.50:2.1": "“Sir, a noble disciple who is sure and devoted to the Realized One would have no doubt or uncertainty about the Realized One or his instructions. ",
  "sn48.50:2.2": "You can expect that a faithful noble disciple will live with energy roused up for giving up unskillful qualities and embracing skillful qualities. They’re strong, staunchly vigorous, not slacking off when it comes to developing skillful qualities. ",
  "sn48.50:2.3": "For their energy is the faculty of energy. ",
  "sn48.50:3.1": "You can expect that a faithful and energetic noble disciple will be mindful, with utmost mindfulness and alertness, able to remember and recall what was said and done long ago. ",
  "sn48.50:3.2": "For their mindfulness is the faculty of mindfulness. ",
  "sn48.50:4.1": "You can expect that a faithful, energetic, and mindful noble disciple will, relying on letting go, gain immersion, gain unification of mind. ",
  "sn48.50:4.2": "For their immersion is the faculty of immersion. ",
  "sn48.5